#: 67e4d895945c4d989f0810db6fa11587
msgid "Reference"
msgstr ""

#: 41a20d9eb90949a795fe521d46637906
msgid ""
"Reference guides are **technical descriptions** of the machinery and how "
"to operate it. Reference material is **information-oriented**."
msgstr ""

#: d9f4941d0c124c549ba056ecdc805992
msgid ""
"Reference material contains *propositional or theoretical* knowledge that"
" a user looks to in their *work*."
msgstr ""

#: 3b151246fc8f403b84c4c841906a1191
msgid ""
"The only purpose of a reference guide is to describe, as succinctly as "
"possible, and in an orderly way. Whereas the content of tutorials and "
"how-to guides are led by needs of the user, reference material is led by "
"the product it describes."
msgstr ""

#: d59a493f4cbf4a98b8a92aef5c831157
msgid ""
"Reference - information oriented, theoretical knowledge, that serves our "
"work"
msgstr ""

#: 79c6b123e7944b77afb440c5a7031738
msgid ""
"In the case of software, reference guides describe the software itself - "
"APIs, classes, functions and so on - and how to use them."
msgstr ""

#: 865a990903bd4a908bb899882ec54169
msgid ""
"Your users need reference material because they need truth and certainty "
"- firm platforms on which to stand while they work. Good technical "
"reference is essential to provide users with the confidence to do their "
"work."
msgstr ""

#: 672c4ce3c4e54a75aa476525a3820f28
msgid "Reference as description"
msgstr ""

#: fdee1fac90bd4ca792a12a7437cb041c
msgid ""
"Reference material describes the machinery. It should be **austere**. One"
" hardly *reads* reference material; one *consults* it."
msgstr ""

#: 8d29a411cc67415d8e5007b2be4520b3
msgid ""
"There should be no doubt or ambiguity in reference; it should be wholly "
"authoritative."
msgstr ""

#: 58756da979e843b0ae23a028cfa67c53
msgid ""
"Reference material is like a map. A map tells you what you need to know "
"about the territory, without having to go out and check the territory for"
" yourself; a reference guide serves the same purpose for the product and "
"its internal machinery."
msgstr ""

#: af81f35a17134e0b8159e883219e94a8
msgid ""
"Although reference should not attempt to show how to perform tasks, it "
"can and often needs to include a description of how something works or "
"the correct way to use it."
msgstr ""

#: 6cfaedd3aa6d4df7b715ad1bfa7aee17
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, too many software developers think that auto-generated "
"reference material is all the documentation required."
msgstr ""

#: 38ba6360547a49a193988c6b13cbb874
msgid ""
"Some reference material (such as API documentation) can be generated "
"automatically by the software it describes, which is a powerful way of "
"ensuring that it remains faithfully accurate to the code."
msgstr ""

#: 8811923ffb454c4a9fb7e3d4e0e11fe4
msgid "Key principles"
msgstr ""

#: 730611ab289746fb9fd7899b3d330dd1
msgid "Describe and only describe"
msgstr ""

#: ca77f237bc654d48983a649ef09bd684
msgid "*Neutral description* is the key imperative of technical reference."
msgstr ""

#: 47c971c7c5e34e169bb23f23a3fb366d
msgid "austere and uncompromising"
msgstr ""

#: f40e7a21197144a89d11906d5d7166bd
msgid "neutrality, objectivity, factuality"
msgstr ""

#: 7f659d9608284ae58bca73d3135bf272
msgid "structured according to the structure of the machinery itself"
msgstr ""

#: e5e79c20f34748528c5402bfc49582cd
msgid ""
"Unfortunately one of the hardest things to do is to describe something "
"neutrally. It's not a natural way of communicating. What's natural on the"
" other hand is to explain, instruct, discuss, opine, and all these things"
" run counter to the needs of technical reference, which instead demands "
"accuracy, precision, completeness and clarity."
msgstr ""

#: ec0b50cab94142a5bc488e5d2d129dd2
msgid ""
"It can be tempting to introduce instruction and explanation, simply "
"because description can seem too inadequate to be useful, and because we "
"do indeed need these other things. Instead, link to how-to guides, "
"explanation and introductory tutorials."
msgstr ""

#: 678d23de01944180a1d8d2f6d2e4c39d
msgid "Adopt standard patterns"
msgstr ""

#: dcc56c98965f46a5aaf117040428985b
msgid ""
"**Reference material is useful when it is consistent.** Standard patterns"
" are what allow us to use reference material effectively. Your job is to "
"place the material that your user needs where they expect to find it, in "
"a format that they are familiar with."
msgstr ""

#: 2ff80a08cfbd478bb3e16069e1beb6ab
msgid ""
"There are many opportunities in writing to delight your readers with your"
" extensive vocabulary and command of multiple styles, but reference "
"material is definitely not one of them."
msgstr ""

#: c2620b51f5704af286721bab88fdd1da
msgid "Respect the structure of the machinery"
msgstr ""

#: 1ea034fabb444b1e9a7003683bbe9481
msgid ""
"The way a map corresponds to the territory it represents helps us use the"
" former to find our way through the latter. It should be the same with "
"documentation: **the structure of the documentation should mirror the "
"structure of the product**, so that the user can work their way through "
"them at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: 1593bd9e53724252a00bd1f65874b72c
msgid ""
"It doesn't mean forcing the documentation into an unnatural structure. "
"What's important is that the logical, conceptual arrangement of and "
"relations within the code should help make sense of the documentation."
msgstr ""

#: f4638cf7b07146a2868462b519ab32b0
msgid "Provide examples"
msgstr ""

#: ab5a44eef4a94c16a8f6a2ce5ffb938f
msgid ""
"**Examples** are valuable ways of providing illustration that helps "
"readers understand reference, while avoiding the risk of becoming "
"distracted from the job of describing. For example, an example of usage "
"of a command can be a succinct way of illustrating it and its context, "
"without falling into the trap of trying to explain or instruct."
msgstr ""

#: ab0d88de4e3a428c85d281ae806f9fea
msgid "The language of reference guides"
msgstr ""

#: a56d8e4a62094595b51b455270ce6990
msgid ""
"Django's default logging configuration inherits Python's defaults. It's "
"available as ``django.utils.log.DEFAULT_LOGGING`` and defined in "
"``django/utils/log.py``"
msgstr ""

#: 294288ccb2ee4067801ff6798362f9bc
msgid "State facts about the machinery and its behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: 6adb3bd316d24eacb21b2e9a40eda1c7
msgid "Sub-commands are: a, b, c, d, e, f."
msgstr ""

#: 9c6b0feb6f5748659180767846f1c698
msgid ""
"List commands, options, operations, features, flags, limitations, error "
"messages, etc."
msgstr ""

#: 27f0b004f83644efb2d89b5799055f40
msgid "You must use a. You must not apply b unless c. Never d."
msgstr ""

#: a34161a6a8464999b98605cbd39f3c38
msgid "Provide warnings where appropriate."
msgstr ""

#: 8d636da19e154db0bb566b1b5b8f60cc
msgid "Applied to food and cooking"
msgstr ""

#: c3a62ce41a0a4c17867839db36f3395f
msgid ""
"You might check the information on a packet of food, in order to help you"
" make a decision about what to do."
msgstr ""

#: 1b2bd23573304f55946810c19b040892
msgid ""
"When you're looking for information - relevant facts - you do not want to"
" be confronted by opinions, speculation, instructions or interpretation."
msgstr ""

#: 5a64ff06554b499293128326db937e73
msgid "Information on the back of a packet of lasagne"
msgstr ""

#: 7dda35e654b44541818a625fb2a848df
msgid ""
"You also expect that information to be presented in standard ways, so "
"that you - when you need to know about something's nutritional "
"properties, how it should be stored, its ingredients, what health "
"implications it might have - can find them quickly, and know you can rely"
" on them."
msgstr ""

#: fbd25e198d0d4883a24842ec75ce1715
msgid ""
"So you expect to see for example: *May contain traces of wheat*. Or: *Net"
" weight: 1000g*."
msgstr ""

#: 669158fd32164b63a192b3bcac72660f
msgid ""
"You will certainly not expect to find for example recipes or marketing "
"claims mixed up with this information; that could be literally dangerous."
msgstr ""

#: 9395967625914595b0339b7e5cd64169
msgid ""
"The way reference material is presented on food products is so important "
"that it's usually governed by law, and the same kind of seriousness "
"should apply to all reference documentation."
msgstr ""

